  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65409,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vulva</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65410,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are mostly young women aged &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;years (mean: 19&nbsp;years; range: 1&ndash;52&nbsp;years) {26076163; 27959583}, with 2&nbsp;cases reported in pregnancy. Presentation is with a progressively growing vulvar mass, most commonly localized to the right labium majus. Serum AFP levels are not consistently elevated.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65411,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Germ cell tumours of the vulva are rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65412,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65413,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Germ cell tumours of the vulva are believed to arise from germ cells in the vulva that persist as the result of error in migration.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65414,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The median size is 4&nbsp;cm {26076163; 27959583}. The border may be demarcated {15790466; 26076163}. The cut surface is solid, greyish-white, and fleshy, with a variegated appearance including haemorrhage and necrosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65415,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Almost all cases represent yolk sac tumour. The tumours show a variety of architectural patterns, with reticular being most common. The tumour cells are large, with hyperchromatic, irregular nuclei; prominent nucleoli; and clear cytoplasm that is positive for AFP, glypican-3 (GPC3), and SALL4. There are PAS-positive intracellular and extracellular hyaline globules. Schiller&ndash;Duval bodies, which resemble fetal glomeruli, can be seen. Rarely, there is an admixed component of other primitive germ cell tumours.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-30T12:19:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65416,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65417,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 399,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:33:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
